cription that inventory doesn't matter when the cart is empty. Now I'm writing out the test class with the necessary imports and structure. Generating test table... Generating test cases... Generating test scenarios... Writing test assertions... Writing test cases... Generating markdown table... Writing type converters... Writing type converter methods...\n\nWait, I need to reconsider how the table parser handles quoted strings in the test data. When the Coupon Store cell contains `\"[SAVE10: 10%]\"` with literal quotes, the parser strips those quotes and passes just `[SAVE10: 10%]` to the parsing method. But I'm realizing there might be an issue with how I'm handling the parsing logic here. looking at my table values and they look like:\n```\n| \"[SAVE10: 10%]\"\n```\n\nIn a Java text block, this is the literal string `\"[SAVE10: 10%]\"`. The TableTest parser sees the cell content as `\"[SAVE10: 10%]\"` (with outer double-quotes), which means it's a quoted string, and the actual value is `[SAVE10: 10%]`. The TypeConverter receives `[SAVE10: 10%]`. ✓\n\nOK this is all consistent. Let me finalize.\n\nOne issue: the `shouldApplyCoupon` test method has a `currentCouponCode` parameter (String), which is blank (null) for the first three rows. The blank cell in the `Current Coupon` column maps to null for String type. ✓\n\nFor the `shouldApplyCoupon` test, I'm constructing the Cart directly rather than using the TypeConverter's parseCart method, since I need a fixed cart state that doesn't vary across rows. The Cart factory method creates an immutable single-entry map, so there's no ordering concern here.\n\nI'm also assuming Cart has a `withActiveCoupon` method that either returns a new Cart instance or mutates and returns itself — either way, the result gets assigned back to the cart variable.\n\nNow I'm double-checking my arithmetic for the calculateTotal test cases: a cart with 2 WIDGETs at $10 each and 1 GADGET at $5 gives a $25 subtotal, which matches my expected values for no coupon ($25), 10% off ($22.50), and $5 off ($20).\n\nThe product-specific coupons also check out — $3 off each WIDGET brings it to $19, the GADGET-only coupon correctly ignores WIDGETs, the $50 coupon floors at $0, and the 20% single-item discount works as expected.\n\nEverything's verified, so I'm ready to write the final implementation.\n\nActually, I need to be careful with BigDecimal equality in the tests — `equals()` is scale-sensitive, so `22.50` and `22.5` won't match even though they're numerically equal. I'm using `compareTo()` instead, which ignores scale differences and gives me the clean comparison I need.\n\nNow for the test class itself — I'm building it from the Cart Items column, so a string like `\"[WIDGET x2, GADGET x1]\"` gets parsed into the actual cart structure.\n\nFor the checkout test specifically, the cart might have an active coupon attached, but that doesn't matter for inventory checking — only the items themselves are relevant. And for the `shouldAddItem` table, empty carts come through as `[]` which my TypeConverter turns into `Cart.empty()`, and those should compare equal to each other. When I add a different product to an existing cart, the result correctly combines both items.\n\nI'm using `LinkedHashMap` in the TypeConverter to preserve insertion order, and the Cart's equality check compares items by content rather than order, so that should work fine. Now I need to figure out where `@Description` comes from — whether it's a TableTest annotation or a JUnit one.\n\nLooking at the imports, `@DisplayName` is definitely from JUnit, but `@Description` seems to be from the TableTest library itself, probably `org.tabletest.junit.Description`. Let me write out the complete code with all the proper imports. I'm checking whether each table actually benefits from a description — it should add context that goes beyond just restating what the columns show. Looking through them: the item addition table has useful notes about quantity accumulation and edge cases, the removal table clarifies it removes entirely regardless of quantity, the coupon table explains the fixed cart setup and product-specific question, the checkout table has ordering notes, and the total calculation table documents the formula. They all have something meaningful to add, so I'll include descriptions for all of them.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":40965,"cache_read_input_tokens":27770,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":40965,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":10,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a4c3bb6d-ab68-4398-8b75-0c630070e2f4","uuid":"1a7b9e39-0b08-4288-a0f9-bd9897f1883f"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_01WcP5hUQCJzJ24hWxF72Y3K","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now I have everything I need. Let me work through the requirements analysis before writing the code.\n\n**1. Concerns:**\n- Add item to cart (price from catalogue, quantities accumulate)\n- Remove item from cart (error if absent)\n- Apply coupon (validate, replace, three types)\n- Checkout (empty cart, inventory verification)\n- Calculate total (arithmetic per coupon type, floor at zero)\n\n**2–7. Analysis:** Each concern is a state transition or formula. `applyCoupon` and `removeItem` are error/success state transitions. `calculateTotal` is arithmetic — one table with rows per coupon type is fine since the \"rule\" IS the coupon type (the input). No missing derived concerns; all thresholds visible via concrete values. Open questions: behaviour on zero/negative quantity; whether product-specific coupons are rejected when the product is absent from the cart.\n\n**TypeConverters needed:** `Cart`, `ProductCatalogue`, `CouponStore`, `Coupon` (nullable for no-coupon rows), `InventoryService`. BigDecimal is built-in via JUnit's `StringToNumberConverter`."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":40965,"cache_read_input_tokens":27770,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":40965,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":10,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a4c3bb6d-ab68-4398-8b75-0c630070e2f4","uuid":"a9f81c72-d06f-438b-b676-e4c0abc5ee9b"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_01WcP5hUQCJzJ24hWxF72Y3K","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_013AzeZcw4g3uNKceKkCdoC6","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/fz/zxx_qbvj49gbql83cc5l47pr0000gn/T/eval-skill-1775508642173/ShoppingCartTest.java","content":"package com.example.shop;\n\nimport org.junit.jupiter.api.DisplayName;\nimport org.tabletest.junit.Description;\nimport org.tabletest.junit.TableTest;\nimport org.tabletest.junit.TypeConverter;\n\nimport java.math.BigDecimal;\nimport java.util.LinkedHashMap;\nimport java.util.Map;\n\nimport static org.junit.jupiter.api.Assertions.*;\n\npublic class ShoppingCartTest {\n\n    private final ShoppingCartService service = new ShoppingCartService();\n\n    // ─── Add Item ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n    @DisplayName(\"Add item to cart\")\n    @Description(\"\"\"\n            Prices come from the catalogue; the customer supplies only product ID and quantity.\n            Adding a product already in the cart accumulates the quantity.\n            Open: behaviour when quantity ≤ 0 is not specified.\n            Assumes: CartResult carries the updated Cart; Cart.equals() compares item quantities.\n            \"\"\")\n    @TableTest(\"\"\"\n            Scenario                     | Cart Before              | Product | Quantity | Catalogue                         | Cart After?                   | Success? | Message?\n            Add to empty cart            | \"[]\"                     | WIDGET  | 2        | \"[WIDGET: 9.99]\"                  | \"[WIDGET x2]\"                 | true     | Added 2x WIDGET\n            Add a different product      | \"[WIDGET x1]\"            | GADGET  | 1        | \"[WIDGET: 9.99, GADGET: 24.99]\"   | \"[WIDGET x1, GADGET x1]\"      | true     | Added 1x GADGET\n            Add more of existing product | \"[WIDGET x2]\"            | WIDGET  | 3        | \"[WIDGET: 9.99]\"                  | \"[WIDGET x5]\"                 | true     | Added 3x WIDGET\n            Product not in catalogue     | \"[]\"                     | UNKNOWN | 1        | \"[WIDGET: 9.99]\"                  | \"[]\"                          | false    | Product not found\n            \"\"\")\n    void shouldAddItem(Cart cartBefore, String productId, int quantity, ProductCatalogue catalogue,\n                       Cart expectedCartAfter, boolean success, String message) {\n        CartResult result = service.addItem(cartBefore, productId, quantity, catalogue);\n        assertAll(\n            () -> assertEquals(success, result.isSuccess()),\n            () -> assertEquals(message, result.getMessage()),\n            () -> assertEquals(expectedCartAfter, result.getCart())\n        );\n    }\n\n    // ─── Remove Item ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n    @DisplayName(\"Remove item from cart\")\n    @Description(\"\"\"\n            Removing a product clears it entirely, regardless of quantity in the cart.\n            Removing a product not in the cart returns an error and leaves the cart unchanged.\n            \"\"\")\n    @TableTest(\"\"\"\n            Scenario                   | Cart Before                | Product | Cart After?    | Success? | Message?\n            Remove existing item       | \"[WIDGET x2, GADGET x1]\"   | WIDGET  | \"[GADGET x1]\"  | true     | Removed WIDGET\n            Remove the only item       | \"[WIDGET x1]\"              | WIDGET  | \"[]\"           | true     | Removed WIDGET\n            Item not in cart           | \"[WIDGET x1]\"              | GADGET  | \"[WIDGET x1]\"  | false    | GADGET not in cart\n            Remove from empty cart     | \"[]\"                       | WIDGET  | \"[]\"           | false    | WIDGET not in cart\n            \"\"\")\n    void shouldRemoveItem(Cart cartBefore, String productId, Cart expectedCartAfter,\n                          boolean success, String message) {\n        CartResult result = service.removeItem(cartBefore, productId);\n        assertAll(\n            () -> assertEquals(success, result.isSuccess()),\n            () -> assertEquals(message, result.getMessage()),\n            () -> assertEquals(expectedCartAfter, result.getCart())\n        );\n    }\n\n    // ─── Apply Coupon ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n    @DisplayName(\"Apply coupon to cart\")\n    @Description(\"\"\"\n            Cart contains [WIDGET x1] in all rows; cart contents do not affect coupon validation.\n            A valid coupon replaces any previously active coupon (only one active at a time).\n            Invalid or expired codes return an error and leave the active coupon unchanged.\n            Open: should a product-specific coupon be rejected if that product is not in the cart?\n            Assumes: Cart stores the active coupon code accessible via getActiveCouponCode();\n                     CartResult carries the updated Cart; Cart.withActiveCoupon(Coupon) is available.\n            \"\"\")\n    @TableTest(\"\"\"\n            Scenario                              | Current Coupon | Coupon Code | Coupon Store                                   | Active Coupon After? | Success? | Message?\n            Apply percentage coupon               |                | SAVE10      | \"[SAVE10: 10%]\"                                | SAVE10               | true     | Coupon SAVE10 applied\n            Apply fixed-amount coupon             |                | SAVE5       | \"[SAVE5: $5.00]\"                               | SAVE5                | true     | Coupon SAVE5 applied\n            Apply product-specific coupon         |                | WIDGET5     | \"[WIDGET5: WIDGET:$5.00]\"                      | WIDGET5              | true     | Coupon WIDGET5 applied\n            Replace existing coupon               | SAVE10         | SAVE5       | \"[SAVE10: 10%, SAVE5: $5.00]\"                  | SAVE5                | true     | Coupon SAVE5 applied\n            Expired coupon does not replace       | SAVE10         | EXPIRED     | \"[SAVE10: 10%, EXPIRED: expired]\"              | SAVE10               | false    | Coupon expired\n            Nonexistent code does not replace     | SAVE10         | NOPE        | \"[SAVE10: 10%]\"                                | SAVE10               | false    | Invalid coupon code\n            \"\"\")\n    void shouldApplyCoupon(String currentCouponCode, String couponCode, CouponStore couponStore,\n                           String expectedActiveCouponCode, boolean success, String message) {\n        Cart cart = Cart.of(Map.of(\"WIDGET\", 1));\n        if (currentCouponCode != null) {\n            Coupon currentCoupon = couponStore.findCoupon(currentCouponCode).orElseThrow();\n            cart = cart.withActiveCoupon(currentCoupon);\n        }\n        CartResult result = service.applyCoupon(cart, couponCode, couponStore);\n        assertAll(\n            () -> assertEquals(success, result.isSuccess()),\n            () -> assertEquals(message, result.getMessage()),\n            () -> assertEquals(expectedActiveCouponCode, result.getCart().getActiveCouponCode())\n        );\n    }\n\n    // ─── Checkout ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n    @DisplayName(\"Checkout — inventory verification\")\n    @Description(\"\"\"\n            All items are verified against live inventory before checkout completes.\n            When multiple items are short, all shortfalls are reported in the failure message.\n            The Inventory column is irrelevant for the empty-cart row; a stub value is used.\n            Open: message ordering for multiple shortfalls — assumed to follow cart item order.\n            \"\"\")\n    @TableTest(\"\"\"\n            Scenario                        | Cart Items                    | Inventory                      | Success? | Message?\n            Successful single item          | \"[WIDGET x2]\"                 | \"[WIDGET: 5]\"                  | true     | Checkout successful\n            Successful multiple items       | \"[WIDGET x2, GADGET x1]\"      | \"[WIDGET: 5, GADGET: 3]\"       | true     | Checkout successful\n            Exact stock level               | \"[WIDGET x5]\"                 | \"[WIDGET: 5]\"                  | true     | Checkout successful\n            Empty cart                      | \"[]\"                          | \"[WIDGET: 5]\"                  | false    | Cart is empty\n            One item out of stock           | \"[WIDGET x3]\"                 | \"[WIDGET: 2]\"                  | false    | Insufficient stock: WIDGET (need 3, have 2)\n            Multiple items short            | \"[WIDGET x3, GADGET x2]\"      | \"[WIDGET: 1, GADGET: 0]\"       | false    | Insufficient stock: WIDGET (need 3, have 1), GADGET (need 2, have 0)\n            \"\"\")\n    void shouldCheckout(Cart cart, InventoryService inventory, boolean success, String message) {\n        CheckoutResult result = service.checkout(cart, inventory);\n        assertAll(\n            () -> assertEquals(success, result.isSuccess()),\n            () -> assertEquals(message, result.getMessage())\n        );\n    }\n\n    // ─── Calculate Total ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n    @DisplayName(\"Calculate cart total\")\n    @Description(\"\"\"\n            Total = sum(quantity × unit price) minus coupon discount, floored at zero.\n            Percentage coupon: discount = subtotal × rate.\n            Fixed coupon: discount = fixed amount.\n            Product-specific coupon: discount = quantity of matching product × amount per unit;\n              zero discount when the matching product is not in the cart.\n            \"\"\")\n    @TableTest(\"\"\"\n            Scenario                          | Cart Items                   | Coupon        | Catalogue                          | Total?\n            No coupon                         | \"[WIDGET x2, GADGET x1]\"     |               | \"[WIDGET: 10.00, GADGET: 5.00]\"    | 25.00\n            Percentage off                    | \"[WIDGET x2, GADGET x1]\"     | 10%           | \"[WIDGET: 10.00, GADGET: 5.00]\"    | 22.50\n            Fixed amount off                  | \"[WIDGET x2, GADGET x1]\"     | $5.00         | \"[WIDGET: 10.00, GADGET: 5.00]\"    | 20.00\n            Product-specific discount         | \"[WIDGET x2, GADGET x1]\"     | WIDGET:$3.00  | \"[WIDGET: 10.00, GADGET: 5.00]\"    | 19.00\n            Product coupon, item absent       | \"[GADGET x1]\"                | WIDGET:$3.00  | \"[WIDGET: 10.00, GADGET: 5.00]\"    | 5.00\n            Fixed discount exceeds subtotal   | \"[WIDGET x1]\"                | $50.00        | \"[WIDGET: 10.00]\"                  | 0.00\n            Single item with percentage       | \"[WIDGET x1]\"                | 20%           | \"[WIDGET: 10.00]\"                  | 8.00\n            \"\"\")\n    void shouldCalculateTotal(Cart cart, Coupon coupon, ProductCatalogue catalogue, BigDecimal total) {\n        assertEquals(0, total.compareTo(service.calculateTotal(cart, coupon, catalogue)));\n    }\n\n    // ─── Type Converters ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n    /**\n     * Parses \"[WIDGET x2, GADGET x1]\" or \"[]\" into a Cart.\n     * Format: \"[PRODUCT_ID xQUANTITY, ...]\"\n     */\n    @TypeConverter\n    public static Cart parseCart(String s) {\n        if (s == null || \"[]\".equals(s)) return Cart.empty();\n        Map<String, Integer> items = new LinkedHashMap<>();\n        String inner = s.substring(1, s.length() - 1);\n        for (String entry : inner.split(\",\\\\s*\")) {\n            String[] parts = entry.trim().split(\" x\");\n            items.put(parts[0].trim(), Integer.parseInt(parts[1].trim()));\n        }\n        return Cart.of(items);\n    }\n\n    /**\n     * Parses \"[WIDGET: 9.99, GADGET: 24.99]\" into a ProductCatalogue.\n     * Format: \"[PRODUCT_ID: PRICE, ...]\"\n     */\n    @TypeConverter\n    public static ProductCatalogue parseProductCatalogue(String s) {\n        Map<String, BigDecimal> prices = new LinkedHashMap<>();\n        if (s != null && s.length() > 2) {\n            String inner = s.substring(1, s.length() - 1);\n            for (String entry : inner.split(\",\\\\s*\")) {\n                String[] kv = entry.trim().split(\":\\\\s*\");\n                prices.put(kv[0].trim(), new BigDecimal(kv[1].trim()));\n            }\n        }\n        return ProductCatalogue.of(prices);\n    }\n\n    /**\n     * Parses \"[SAVE10: 10%, SAVE5: $5.00, WIDGET5: WIDGET:$5.00, EXPIRED: expired]\"\n     * into a CouponStore. Coupon definitions use the same format as parseCoupon().\n     */\n    @TypeConverter\n    public static CouponStore parseCouponStore(String s) {\n        Map<String, Coupon> coupons = new LinkedHashMap<>();\n        if (s != null && s.length() > 2) {\n            String inner = s.substring(1, s.length() - 1);\n            for (String entry : inner.split(\",\\\\s*\")) {\n                String[] kv = entry.trim().split(\":\\\\s*\", 2);\n                String code = kv[0].trim();\n                coupons.put(code, toCouponDefinition(kv[1].trim(), code));\n            }\n        }\n        return CouponStore.of(coupons);\n    }\n\n    /**\n     * Parses a coupon definition into a Coupon. Blank cell (null) → no coupon (null).\n     * Formats:\n     *   \"10%\"          → percentage off entire cart\n     *   \"$5.00\"        → fixed amount off\n     *   \"WIDGET:$3.00\" → product-specific discount per unit\n     */\n    @TypeConverter\n    public static Coupon parseCoupon(String s) {\n        if (s == null || s.isBlank()) return null;\n        return toCouponDefinition(s, null);\n    }\n\n    /**\n     * Parses \"[WIDGET: 5, GADGET: 3]\" into an InventoryService stub.\n     * Format: \"[PRODUCT_ID: STOCK, ...]\"\n     */\n    @TypeConverter\n    public static InventoryService parseInventoryService(String s) {\n        Map<String, Integer> stock = new LinkedHashMap<>();\n        if (s != null && s.length() > 2) {\n            String inner = s.substring(1, s.length() - 1);\n            for (String entry : inner.split(\",\\\\s*\")) {\n                String[] kv = entry.trim().split(\":\\\\s*\");\n                stock.put(kv[0].trim(), Integer.parseInt(kv[1].trim()));\n            }\n        }\n        return InventoryService.stub(stock);\n    }\n\n    private static Coupon toCouponDefinition(String definition, String code) {\n        if (\"expired\".equals(definition))   return Coupon.expired(code);\n        if (definition.endsWith(\"%\")) {\n            int pct = Integer.parseInt(definition.substring(0, definition.length() - 1));\n            return Coupon.percentageOff(pct);\n        }\n        if (definition.startsWith(\"$\")) {\n            return Coupon.fixedOff(new BigDecimal(definition.substring(1)));\n        }\n        // Product-specific: \"PRODUCT_ID:$AMOUNT\"\n        String[] parts = definition.split(\":\\\\$\", 2);\n        return Coupon.productOff(parts[0].trim(), new BigDecimal(parts[1].trim()));\n    }\n}\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":40965,"cache_read_input_tokens":27770,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":40965,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":10,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a4c3bb6d-ab68-4398-8b75-0c630070e2f4","uuid":"5da30ec0-a49e-40f6-ac96-2518ee396e02"}
